{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis","id":1031969,"title":"Playing Lupus & Metis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-14T21:04:21-08:00","id":1031969,"title":"Playing Lupus & Metis","content":"I know there's a book coming out that's supposed to touch on this (Changing Ways?), but until that's released I wanted stir up some discussion on playing characters born outside of human society. I'll post up my thoughts on playing them later once I've mulled over it some more.<br /> <br /> <b>Lupus</b><br /> Many games I've stumbled across online outright ban lupus, usually on some account that they're 'snowflakes,' draw in weird roleplayers, or that they are too difficult to play/don't fit in. <a href=\"http://garoumush.wikia.com/wiki/Lupus_Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Guides like this</a> imply that they're dimwitted (although their writing on the cognitive abilities of wolves seems questionable at best) and that it's unrealistic for a lupus character to speak competently or even grasp human cultures without a decade of study.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? How do you think lupus are best played? If you ban them from your games, why?<br /> <br /> <b>Metis</b><br /> Another one that might be tough to portray. Not only raised up in an alien culture, but one that almost universally despises them for what they are, all while dealing with Rage from birth. I've not seen them banned as much as lupus, but they're often restricted.<br /> <br /> Same questions as before.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://discord.gg/pte7kB6\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Moon Sept</a>, a discord server for fans of Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12874-mongoose","name":"Mongoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12874_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T21:30:01-08:00","id":1031975,"title":"","content":"Well, I tend to restrict lupus characters to experience players and forbid metis characters because I do not want to deal with the social issues. With the changes reported from W20, the ratio of homid-to-lupus is 8:1, and I imagine that the metis are even rarer than the lupus because they are forbidden by the Litany, so I generally use a lupus-to-homid ratio of 8:1, so the homid-lupis-metis ratio in my games are 64:8:1. Certain groups (Black Spiral Dancers and Hakken) will reverse the proportion of Metis and Lupus, and I think that I would allow a metis in a Hakken game, since the Hakken belong to the Beast Courts rather than the Garou Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T00:06:43-08:00","id":1032025,"title":"","content":"Lupus Garou are not wolves just as homid Garou are not humans. Lupus characters obviously do not have the benefit of a dozen or so years living among humans, but neither are they animals. I don't penalize lupus characters adapting to human cultures any more than I penalize homid characters from being able to act likes wolves.<br /> <br /> The spirit half of the Garou can be used to explain a fairly quick adaption to humanity. While the few players I've had of lupus characters have wanted to play rather direct and guileless characters, neither were they dimwitted. They may not understand the complexities of human society, but they can speak normally in human tongue by the time they are Cliath. Any limitations they have are because of how the PC wants them to be.<br /> <br /> One wants to see the differences between the breeds, but not to the point where lupus characters cannot interact with humanity and &quot;pass&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think the main reason for such guides is to prevent players from picking lupus simply to get the 5 Gnosis and not really wanting to play an alien mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T03:41:52-08:00","id":1032069,"title":"","content":"I definitely fall into the camp that a Lupus is gonna be struggling to do anything that's too human for them atleast until they hit fostern and have had to deal with a bunch of homids.<br /> <br /> I don't begrudge players that find the idea frustrating and try to minimize it but I'm just left wondering what's the bloody point of playing one then.<br /> <br /> As for metis, depends on the tribe how prevalent they are and how they'll be treated (mostly like shit though). Big thing I do like to bring up is the stigma that metis turn to the wyrm in droves compared to the other breeds (admitedly that is because of how horrible their lives get, but that's the beauty of werewolf: Garou are cunts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T03:50:55-08:00","id":1032072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032025#post1032025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main reason for such guides is to prevent players from picking lupus simply to get the 5 Gnosis and not really wanting to play an alien mindset.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on the nature of the game in question, lupus are equally likely to be banned/restricted under the justification of keeping them rare as the setting dictates; since such rulings usually come out of larger group play instead of normal TT group sized play. The frequency of this in such games is definitely the combination of these two factors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T03:58:09-08:00","id":1032074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cantankerous Bees</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032069#post1032069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't begrudge players that find the idea frustrating and try to minimize it but I'm just left wondering what's the bloody point of playing one then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personal example?<br /> <br /> One of my lupus Philodox PCs spent a lot of his time training to become a Cliath working on being able to pass as human so he could understand the homids he was going to be expected to be able to be a judge over. It was his duty to Gaia to fulfill his Auspice's role by being able to put himself in a homid's shoes. It also made him that much better at representing his lupus packmate that completely disagreed with the value in such things to all the homids that also weren't getting deep in touch with their wolf-side.<br /> <br /> The point of playing a lupus that can pass as a homid is... because they're still passing even if convincingly. Passing isn't the same as being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T04:17:31-08:00","id":1032078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032074#post1032074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personal example?<br /> <br /> One of my lupus Philodox PCs spent a lot of his time training to become a Cliath working on being able to pass as human so he could understand the homids he was going to be expected to be able to be a judge over. It was his duty to Gaia to fulfill his Auspice's role by being able to put himself in a homid's shoes. It also made him that much better at representing his lupus packmate that completely disagreed with the value in such things to all the homids that also weren't getting deep in touch with their wolf-side.<br /> <br /> The point of playing a lupus that can pass as a homid is... because they're still passing even if convincingly. Passing isn't the same as being.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair counterpoint, and it sounds like a good character arc for a lupus (It should probably be mentioned I normally play/run from first change onwards).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:30:55-08:00","id":1032201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mongoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis#post1031969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Lupus</b><br /> Many games I've stumbled across online outright ban lupus, usually on some account that they're 'snowflakes,' draw in weird roleplayers, or that they are too difficult to play/don't fit in. <a href=\"http://garoumush.wikia.com/wiki/Lupus_Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Guides like this</a> imply that they're dimwitted (although their writing on the cognitive abilities of wolves seems questionable at best) and that it's unrealistic for a lupus character to speak competently or even grasp human cultures without a decade of study.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? How do you think lupus are best played? If you ban them from your games, why?<br /> <br /> <b>Metis</b><br /> Another one that might be tough to portray. Not only raised up in an alien culture, but one that almost universally despises them for what they are, all while dealing with Rage from birth. I've not seen them banned as much as lupus, but they're often restricted.<br /> <br /> Same questions as before.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That Lupus guide seems terrible. I didn't get much past the first couple of paragraphs though, so many it gets better (doubtful). Personally, I've never had an issue with Lupus players. There are some general guidelines, but playing Lupus shouldn't be outright banned imo. If a player wants to play one, I usually go over why they want to and what they thinking coming from the Lupus breed will add to their concept. If the character sounds interesting and they aren't choosing Lupus simply for the higher Gnosis, then there is no issue. Lupus characters tend to be more direct in their approaches (a broad generalization), but that doesn't make them stupid by any means. And the human culture thing isn't a big deal. If you are playing a game where the character start out at Rank 1, then the Lupus will have already gone through their introduction to human society, prior to their Rite of Passage. They should be as good on 2 legs as Homids are on 4 by that point, which is to say: passable.<br /> <br /> For Metis, the only requirement I tend to have is that the player needs to be previously familiar with the Werewolf setting. If you are going to play a character that grew up their whole life in the Garou Nation, then the player should have some understanding of the Garou Nation and what they are getting into playing a Metis. And again, the question of what this Breed brings to their character concept. If I have a completely new player that really wants to play a Metis (its only happened once), I asked them to play a Homid for the first part of the game to get a feel for it and then they retired the character later once they knew more about how Garou society works.<br /> <br /> In any case, I have never understood the heavy restrictions/outright bans that some STs put on playing these Breeds.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T11:03:41-08:00","id":1032216,"title":"","content":"Well, when a player plays a character who began as an animal, I want them to be able to ropleplay someone who is still occasionally confused and frustrated with human society despite having a few years of practice. Just think about dating, it really takes most people years of dating practice before they start to understand the needs of their partners (and some people require decades of practice). Now, most lupus are probably not going to be doing much dating, but it is an example of how players should understand the confusion and frustration that lupus characters should experience with human society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T11:13:52-08:00","id":1032227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032216#post1032216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, when a player plays a character who began as an animal, I want them to be able to ropleplay someone who is still occasionally confused and frustrated with human society despite having a few years of practice. Just think about dating, it really takes most people years of dating practice before they start to understand the needs of their partners (and some people require decades of practice). Now, most lupus are probably not going to be doing much dating, but it is an example of how players should understand the confusion and frustration that lupus characters should experience with human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this completely. Though the Lupus Breed character does at least have a baseline to start from.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen about how some view Lupus, they think the Breed should be 100% lost when it comes to humans. Seemingly solely for the reason that they were not born human. And that I disagree with. Same as a Homid is going to run into some social issues when it comes to wolves. That doesn't mean they don't have at least a rudimentary understanding of what's going on. Since in both case, the being is half-human/half-wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T14:40:37-08:00","id":1032330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032216#post1032216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, when a player plays a character who began as an animal, I want them to be able to ropleplay someone who is still occasionally confused and frustrated with human society despite having a few years of practice. Just think about dating, it really takes most people years of dating practice before they start to understand the needs of their partners (and some people require decades of practice). Now, most lupus are probably not going to be doing much dating, but it is an example of how players should understand the confusion and frustration that lupus characters should experience with human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to give a lot of leeway in how this plays out though.<br /> <br /> Dating oddly came up with the character I was discussing earlier. He wasn't particularly confused by human dating. He was confused that homids would continue to try to follow those ideas with their kin when Garou are capable of skipping all of that. He determined that human mating as naturally inefficient and difficult because humans reproduce so easily they have to do a lot to impress mates, but he also felt it was generally very ease to figure out if two humans were a decent couple because he would just watch their body language and ignore all the wordy cultural baggage.<br /> <br /> There can be a lot of nuance here besides, &quot;humans are confusing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T15:16:23-08:00","id":1032344,"title":"","content":"I have a concept for a Lupus character that figured out homid mating as &quot;Give her food, listen to her talk, make her laugh, and hope she invites you in&quot;.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately he neglected to mention to his metis grandson that if she doesn't invite you in, to move on to the next female. So this poor metis is stuck in the freind zone. But as a metis, he's used to not getting what he wants.<br /> <br /> Also had a homid be very confused as to why this wolf kin kept nipping at him. &quot;obviously she didn't want me around, but when I ran away she kept following me.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot; did you smell her ass? &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot; why would I smell her ass? &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot; to see if she was in heat. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> <br /> I guess my point is, sex is confusing for all breeds. And it is possible for all breeds to figure out the mating habits of one of the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-15-2017, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T18:56:44-08:00","id":1032425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mongoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis#post1031969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know there's a book coming out that's supposed to touch on this (Changing Ways?), but until that's released I wanted stir up some discussion on playing characters born outside of human society. I'll post up my thoughts on playing them later once I've mulled over it some more.<br /> <br /> <b>Lupus</b><br /> Many games I've stumbled across online outright ban lupus, usually on some account that they're 'snowflakes,' draw in weird roleplayers, or that they are too difficult to play/don't fit in. <a href=\"http://garoumush.wikia.com/wiki/Lupus_Guide\" target=\"_blank\">Guides like this</a> imply that they're dimwitted (although their writing on the cognitive abilities of wolves seems questionable at best) and that it's unrealistic for a lupus character to speak competently or even grasp human cultures without a decade of study.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? How do you think lupus are best played? If you ban them from your games, why?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That guide is seriously terrible. And a reason why I started trying to get lupus being more worldly in games in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> I have two writings where I try to tackle how to play either breed;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/150682893784/anas-guide-to-playing-lupus\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/150682893784/anas-guide-to-playing-lupus\" target=\"_blank\"> Not found. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/150682893784/anas-guide-to-playing-lupus\" target=\"_blank\"> http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/150682893784/anas-guide-to-playing-lupus </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/151064038049/how-to-portrayplay-a-metis\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/151064038049/how-to-portrayplay-a-metis\" target=\"_blank\"> Not found. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/151064038049/how-to-portrayplay-a-metis\" target=\"_blank\"> http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/151064038049/how-to-portrayplay-a-metis </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T06:01:13-08:00","id":1032609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the few players I've had of lupus characters have wanted to play rather direct and guileless characters, neither were they dimwitted. </div> </div> </div> Precisely how I wanted to word it. A Lupus is probably going to view the world through the eyes of an animal. But animals aren't necessarily dumb. A human doesn't really know how to track a scent trail and participate in pack hunting like a wolf (not saying a Homid doesn't adapt to that as well). I've had a bad experience with a Lupus player before, so I kind of get the worry some ST's might have. But generally find them workable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:35:17-08:00","id":1032650,"title":"","content":"So... What potential issues would a Metis have to deal with if they grew up in an &quot;Ideal&quot; situation? By ideal situation, I mean grew up in an Accepting Tribe with loving caregivers. <br /> <br /> 1. They are still rage-filled monsters with teeth and claws. Toddlers can be difficult to deal with during a temper tantrum. I can't imagine having to deal with a toddler killing machine.<br /> <br /> 2. They are being raised by rage-filled monsters. Normal parents can loose their temper raising their children. I can see a situation with a young metis escalate to both parent and child in frenzy.<br /> <br /> 3. Kinfolk could be injured. A solution for problem two is to have a kinfolk involved in the raising of the metis child. Of course you run in to problem one. Kinfolk are more vulnerable than Garou. A metis may have guilt about hurting/killing someone they loved. <br /> <br /> 4. Helicopter parenting. I could see a Garou parents who loves their metis child wish to protect them from poor treatment from the rest of the Garou Nation. While the metis wishes to join their own pack and live their own life, the parent would want their metis child to stay in their pack. <br /> <br /> 5. Learned Helplessness. This is a problem with children with disabilities. I can see this also happen to a Metis. <br /> <br /> 6. Self Hatred. A metis child isn't stupid. They are fully aware what their guardians/parents gave up to raise them. They know that their birth had a negative impact on their parent's standing in the Garou Nation. You could tell a child that it isn't their fault, but children will still blame themselves. <br /> <br /> 7. Identifying with another breed. A Garou parent may want to prepare their metis child for their first change. Teach them how to be human/wolf. I can see a Garou parent going overboard to the point where a metis would think of themselves more as homid/lupus than metis. They may hate other metis for reminding them of who they truly are.<br /> <br /> 8. Lack of social skills. Metis still need to be kept away from society. You could home school them. Let them run though the sept territory, but odds are they will not have anyone their own age to interact with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:50:53-08:00","id":1032656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032650#post1032650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4. Helicopter parenting. I could see a Garou parents who loves their metis child wish to protect them from poor treatment from the rest of the Garou Nation. While the metis wishes to join their own pack and live their own life, the parent would want their metis child to stay in their pack.<br /> <br /> 5. Learned Helplessness. This is a problem with children with disabilities. I can see this also happen to a Metis.<br /> <br /> 6. Self Hatred. A metis child isn't stupid. They are fully aware what their guardians/parents gave up to raise them. They know that their birth had a negative impact on their parent's standing in the Garou Nation. You could tell a child that it isn't their fault, but children will still blame themselves.<br /> <br /> 8. Lack of social skills. Metis still need to be kept away from society. You could home school them. Let them run though the sept territory, but odds are they will not have anyone their own age to interact with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man. A friend of mine played a Metis in a game that was a chore to interact with. She was a great character from a story perspective, teetering beautifully between between arrogantly dismissing all of us Wyrmbringers and talking about how worthless she was and what a terrible burden she must be to us all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:56:08-08:00","id":1032660,"title":"","content":"9. They lack a true connection to either side of the garou and have no 'me' form that isn't a warform.<br /> <br /> 10. They do not share humanity's morality or taboos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:57:04-08:00","id":1032663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032656#post1032656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man. A friend of mine played a Metis in a game that was a chore to interact with. She was a great character from a story perspective, teetering beautifully between between arrogantly dismissing all of us Wyrmbringers and talking about how worthless she was and what a terrible burden she must be to us all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't use my list as a check list for a single metis character. Dear lord, that would be painful to play as and with. I'd pick an idea or two to focus on and maybe touch on one or two more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:15:18-08:00","id":1032675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032656#post1032656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man. A friend of mine played a Metis in a game that was a chore to interact with. She was a great character from a story perspective, teetering beautifully between between arrogantly dismissing all of us Wyrmbringers and talking about how worthless she was and what a terrible burden she must be to us all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think every player of any sort of character needs to make sure others WANT to interact with. Otherwise, so much of their story is not told because no one wants to suffer through the play to hear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:23:15-08:00","id":1032679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032675#post1032675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think every player of any sort of character needs to make sure others WANT to interact with. Otherwise, so much of their story is not told because no one wants to suffer through the play to hear it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen this come up more than a few times, where a player has a detailed backstory and wants to explore it but they make interacting with their character such a chore that the other players just give up trying shortly in.<br /> <br /> Also, while I may not agree with 100% of what's in your guides, they are well done and I think would be a big help for newer players. Good job. I will probably forward players to them if and when I get a Werewolf game up and running again (I'm assuming you don't mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-16-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:28:39-08:00","id":1032684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032679#post1032679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen this come up more than a few times, where a player has a detailed backstory and wants to explore it but they make interacting with their character such a chore that the other players just give up trying shortly in.<br /> <br /> Also, while I may not agree with 100% of what's in your guides, they are well done and I think would be a big help for newer players. Good job. I will probably forward players to them if and when I get a Werewolf game up and running again (I'm assuming you don't mind).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, its like a role in a play. You need to make sure others WANT to watch you, want to see more of you.<br /> <br /> As for my guides, thank you. And I am absolutely cool with you using them.<br /> <br /> What parts do you disagree with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T08:54:50-08:00","id":1032691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032684#post1032684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What parts do you disagree with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe a metis would not share humanity's taboos and morals. It will depend on how that particular metis are raised. For Example, a metis raised by homids may feel stealing is wrong.<br /> <br /> Now those morals will be filtered though different mindset. A metis may feel stealing is wrong, but see no problem with breaking in a place, taking what they need, and leaving something (cash or maybe a dead deer) behind in exchange. Because that is not stealing....that's barter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:37:04-08:00","id":1032722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032684#post1032684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What parts do you disagree with?</div> </div> </div> </div>There really wasn't anything big. I've reread them twice now and I think they are very well put together.<br /> <br /> The part on the Metis section that describes 2 extremes for Metis doesn't give much input for playing one somewhere in between. And yes I know the players can (and probably should) read through Tribe books to get additional information. And on the abuse thing, I think the advice of looking up information on children brought up in abusive homes could be helpful to inform the character, but I wouldn't push it as something I expect a player to do.<br /> <br /> The Lupus section says to describe your behavior and then follow up with saying what it means. I find that in tabletop, most players I've seen tend to default to simply saying that they are speaking in Lupus and then relay what it is they mean, especially after a session or 2 of describing yips and body language. In a play by post game, I can see that going over better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:47:07-08:00","id":1032732,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B007EDOLJ2/ref=dp-kindle-redirect?_encoding=UTF8&amp;btkr=1\" target=\"_blank\">Far from the Tree</a> may be a good starting point for how a Garou Parent may think of their metis child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:06:14-08:00","id":1032861,"title":"","content":"I wrote a really long post about playing a lupus in another threat, so I'm just going to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/889346\">link that here</a> rather than repost it. I disagree that lupus characters should be banned, or that they are not as functional as other breeds. ALL garou have a learning curve after their first change. A homid learning how to be in tune with gnosis, navigate the spirit world, and/or embrace their wolf instincts isn't easy either. Furthermore, all garou are literally made for a purpose, both in general as a changing breed and per their auspice. Certain things will come naturally to them because of that. Lastly, lupus are <i>fucking important. </i>Garou are as much wolf as human, and if they lose the that side of them completely, the ramifications will be huge. If lupus as a breed die out and garou lose their wolf kinfolk, in my opinion, they will begin to lose the wolf form itself. Their spiritual connection to the natural world and the very meaning of what it is to be part wolf will eventually be lost to them. One ability that I think describes this is <b>Primal Urge</b>. Homid have to <i>learn</i> how to use and trust the feral side of their nature, and doing so has a direct impact on their ability to change forms on top of the other uses of the ability. Lupus are their biggest link to that. Now, sure, all this doesn't necessarily mean that the breed is easy to play. I would agree that it isn't for everyone, especially new players. But if the breed and its significance is ignored or left out completely? You're missing out on a huge chunk of the game and what it means to be garou, and you're just playing humans with super powers. Lupus present a challenge, but an interesting and worthwhile one in my opinion. <br /> <br /> Metis is another issue entirely, and I have very conflicted feelings on them as a breed. Mainly, I hate how they are handled in the game in terms of having deformities and being socially ostracized. While the parallels between metis and people who are disabled, have mental health issues, or are otherwise stigmatized socially can make for interesting commentary, the overlay of sin and spiritual corruption and whatnot is just kind of too far for me. While I get that its a great example of how awful garou can be, the fact that there are so many holes in the logic surrounding them and so much willingness to eschew critical thinking in favor of blind hatred just drives me crazy. It's realistic... garou ARE fanatics. I just... bleh. At some point garou are painted in such a horrible light that it feels impossible to cast them as protagonists at all, World of Darkness or not. Their self-righteousness becomes TOO intolerable given their cumulative history of being murderous, stupid, unrepentant fuck-ups. <br /> <br /> I admit that it's also personal. The themes hit too close to home for how carelessly I feel they are handled (both by the game and many storytellers and players), so its just not my cup of tea most of the time. I feel inclined to ban them from future games, and sometimes consider writing them out completely. The pros generally don't outweigh the cons for me.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I think the breed has potential if approached from a particular angle. I personally like to attribute the existence of metis to the effects of the Wyld. Garou have a stronger connection with the Wyld than the other parts of the triat on a very fundamental level, and some definitely tribes acknowledge this. Their very nature as shapeshifters is wyld-ish. My head-canon is that metis come about because when two garou procreate, the wyld energy from both of them becomes too concentrated and mutates the offspring. The resulting metis has some flaws to reflect this, and are just a little less stable in general - which could even mean that their mutable nature is more susceptible to wyrm taint, sure. But the upside is the potential to embrace that Wyld energy and use it. The metis breed gifts really scream this to me. If I were playing a metis, I would make it a point of the character to explore that connection. A male metis Black Fury would be super interesting specifically because of that, given the tribe's reverence for the Wyld. Even then you can't get away from them being treated like shit, but at least it gives you something else to focus on. <br /> <br /> I will also say one last thing about Metis and rage... dealing with something from birth doesn't mean you are less capable of dealing with it as an adult; many times the opposite. If a metis has made it through childhood and adolescence, on through their first change and rite of passage, without getting themselves killed because of their Rage, even while being harassed and abused, I'd bet they have a <i>better</i> mastery on their Rage than a comparable garou of another breed. It takes a lot of willpower to deal with Rage for that long and not snap under the pressure of being treated horribly. Many metis <i>don't</i> make it - but the ones that do, the ones that players would play, should have their shit together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3533-sonofgaia","name":"SonOfGaia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:10:23-08:00","id":1032868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfGaia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032861#post1032861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will also say one last thing about Metis and rage... dealing with something from birth doesn't mean you are less capable of dealing with it as an adult; many times the opposite. If a metis has made it through childhood and adolescence, on through their first change and rite of passage, without getting themselves killed because of their Rage, even while being harassed and abused, I'd bet they have a <i>better</i> mastery on their Rage than a comparable garou of another breed. It takes a lot of willpower to deal with Rage for that long and not snap under the pressure of being treated horribly. Many metis <i>don't</i> make it - but the ones that do, the ones that players would play, should have their shit together.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of head canon this for most metis characters. I got a metis character sheet with the Calm Heart merit for this very reason. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:15:43-08:00","id":1033196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfGaia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032861#post1032861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote a really long post about playing a lupus in another threat, so I'm just going to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/node/889346\">link that here</a> rather than repost it. I disagree that lupus characters should be banned, or that they are not as functional as other breeds. ALL garou have a learning curve after their first change. A homid learning how to be in tune with gnosis, navigate the spirit world, and/or embrace their wolf instincts isn't easy either. Furthermore, all garou are literally made for a purpose, both in general as a changing breed and per their auspice. Certain things will come naturally to them because of that. Lastly, lupus are <i>fucking important. </i>Garou are as much wolf as human, and if they lose the that side of them completely, the ramifications will be huge. If lupus as a breed die out and garou lose their wolf kinfolk, in my opinion, they will begin to lose the wolf form itself. Their spiritual connection to the natural world and the very meaning of what it is to be part wolf will eventually be lost to them. One ability that I think describes this is <b>Primal Urge</b>. Homid have to <i>learn</i> how to use and trust the feral side of their nature, and doing so has a direct impact on their ability to change forms on top of the other uses of the ability. Lupus are their biggest link to that. Now, sure, all this doesn't necessarily mean that the breed is easy to play. I would agree that it isn't for everyone, especially new players. But if the breed and its significance is ignored or left out completely? You're missing out on a huge chunk of the game and what it means to be garou, and you're just playing humans with super powers. Lupus present a challenge, but an interesting and worthwhile one in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with most of this. Especially on lupus' role in the setting as counterpoints to homids, and having them banned basically makes the game humans with superpowers. That actually was the case in Werewolf the Forsaken 1st edition, where NPCs ended up sounding less like werewolves and more like shamans. Their wolf forms were not described nor was there a focus on what made these characters werewolves (seriously, tribe of the moon has such a great example of this) rather than just magic users.<br /> <br /> I also think that a lot of STs overblow the difficulty of playing lupus, in the end it should be as hard or easy as the tone of the game needs it to be. You still have to have a character that is not a millstone dragging the play down, regardless how accurate you want to be. And the GarouMUSH guide linked above gives out exactly the kind of characters that are millstones in the long run. It also ironically makes the garou seem like idiots regarding the Veil and basic education when it comes to lupus. A cliath lupus should be aware how to keep the veil and how to handle tribal things without being a burden.<br /> <br /> Another reason why lupus might be avoided could just be that people are uncomfortable with the idea of them. There is this weird fear of anthromorphic animals lately, and I think a lot of people are being paranoid over it for nothing. Sexual stuff appears only if you want it to appear in your game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfGaia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1032861#post1032861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Metis is another issue entirely, and I have very conflicted feelings on them as a breed. Mainly, I hate how they are handled in the game in terms of having deformities and being socially ostracized. While the parallels between metis and people who are disabled, have mental health issues, or are otherwise stigmatized socially can make for interesting commentary, the overlay of sin and spiritual corruption and whatnot is just kind of too far for me. While I get that its a great example of how awful garou can be, the fact that there are so many holes in the logic surrounding them and so much willingness to eschew critical thinking in favor of blind hatred just drives me crazy. It's realistic... garou ARE fanatics. I just... bleh. At some point garou are painted in such a horrible light that it feels impossible to cast them as protagonists at all, World of Darkness or not. Their self-righteousness becomes TOO intolerable given their cumulative history of being murderous, stupid, unrepentant fuck-ups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, never ever seen in play that people would take the metis abuse in-game too far.<br /> <br /> For me, it is not as much metis' origins or abuse that is the issue with them. It is the lack of other players always wanting to actually confront them beyond offering my characters support and pats on the back. Or trying to tell my characters they should not be afraid. When the characters in question might be ok in their place at the bottom and content with it. Accepting that often seems very hard for some players, I've noticed.<br /> <br /> Metis are an interesting thing, though. I do one day wish to know thepoint of them existing in the game, because from the earlier books, I always got a feeling they were the Igor or generally the ugly outcast.<br /> <br /> The way I write metis histories, I tend to go by real life examples of child abuse or children who were somehow outcasts. And yes it includes at times awful stuff, but it is confronting these things being as likely as support that I often go for.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:30:37-08:00","id":1033447,"title":"","content":"I generally have interpreted the social consequences of bearing a Metis as a way for the Garou Nation to subtly encourage abortion or exposure. On the case of abortion, I imagine that there are Human Kinfolk who will take care of the problem. In the case of exposure, I imagine that there are Wolf Kinfolk who will do the same. Therefore, I imagine that the only Garou who bear and raise Metis children are the ones who either have no choice or who are willing to accept the shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T06:59:44-08:00","id":1033989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1033447#post1033447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally have interpreted the social consequences of bearing a Metis as a way for the Garou Nation to subtly encourage abortion or exposure. On the case of abortion, I imagine that there are Human Kinfolk who will take care of the problem. In the case of exposure, I imagine that there are Wolf Kinfolk who will do the same. Therefore, I imagine that the only Garou who bear and raise Metis children are the ones who either have no choice or who are willing to accept the shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly have to disagree with this. For one, aborting a metis would be an extremely traumatic thing and could easily result the mother dying or becoming infertile. Metis regenerate from birth, after all.<br /> <br /> Second, I don't think most tribes would actually allow abortion even if it was possible.The parents did a consious thing to break the law, even -knowing- the results. To perform an abortion is to say they want to dodge consequences of their sin. Not make up for it, dodge it. To make up for it, the mother could go on a suicide mission or raise the child to serve Gaia. In cases of rape, where I honestly doubt judgement would be levied on the victim, the mother could just do a ritual suicide to avoid the child. Or do a suicide mission, as stated before.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:23:01-08:00","id":1033993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1033989#post1033989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly have to disagree with this. For one, aborting a metis would be an extremely traumatic thing and could easily result the mother dying or becoming infertile. Metis regenerate from birth, after all.<br /> <br /> Second, I don't think most tribes would actually allow abortion even if it was possible.The parents did a consious thing to break the law, even -knowing- the results. To perform an abortion is to say they want to dodge consequences of their sin. Not make up for it, dodge it. To make up for it, the mother could go on a suicide mission or raise the child to serve Gaia. In cases of rape, where I honestly doubt judgement would be levied on the victim, the mother could just do a ritual suicide to avoid the child. Or do a suicide mission, as stated before.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree Garou would not openly support abortion. Secretly supporting exposure/abortion would vary based on tribe. Most will lean towards &quot;Too risky to try&quot;. Others (ironically, the tribes that strongly punish both parent and child) may take the risk and go &quot;the only mortal abortion is my abortion&quot; route. Of course, if you get caught, it will be a larger renown hit.<br /> <br /> I wonder how many CoG/Bonegnawer septs find Metis pups left on their doorstep. Is there rituals to figure out the parents of the child? Do you think CoG would perform the ritual and finger the parents?<br /> <br /> I don't think Garou would encourage the mother to go on Suicide missions either. Mostly because <i>someone</i> has to raise the Metis Child.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-18-2017, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:28:18-08:00","id":1033996,"title":"","content":"It really would not matter if Metis regenerate from birth because, while they are in their mother, they are yet to be born and so their regeneration capability would have yet to be triggered. I really doubt that Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, or Children of Gaia would be against abortion since it would be about the personal freedom of the woman involved (it would also mean that the mother would not be wasting time bearing a Metis that they could use to bear a proper Garou). Garou do not follow human religions for the most part, so they would not have religious reasons to oppose abortion (in fact, they would have a religious argument for aborting a Metis, as Metis are unnatural things whose existence violates the Litany and inhibits the ability of the Garou to protect Gaia because Metis are incapable of producing future Garou to protect Gaia).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:43:29-08:00","id":1034007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1033996#post1033996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really would not matter if Metis regenerate from birth because, while they are in their mother, they are yet to be born and so their regeneration capability would have yet to be triggered. I really doubt that Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, or Children of Gaia would be against abortion since it would be about the personal freedom of the woman involved (it would also mean that the mother would not be wasting time bearing a Metis that they could use to bear a proper Garou). Garou do not follow human religions for the most part, so they would not have religious reasons to oppose abortion (in fact, they would have a religious argument for aborting a Metis, as Metis are unnatural things whose existence violates the Litany and inhibits the ability of the Garou to protect Gaia because Metis are incapable of producing future Garou to protect Gaia).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually say they regenerate from womb. Since the First Law is so important that its the -first- law, it has to have been a serious enough case to put it out there. And in older books, it was said metis were born alien chestburster style, so I'd say a pregnancy with a metis is in itself very unnatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:12:04-08:00","id":1034336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1033993#post1033993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how many CoG/Bonegnawer septs find Metis pups left on their doorstep. Is there rituals to figure out the parents of the child? Do you think CoG would perform the ritual and finger the parents?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's the Rite of Heritage, which can tell your parentage up to X successes per generation; e.g., two successes would reveal your parents &amp; grandparents. As for if they'd track down the parents, I suppose it depends on the Coggies involved. I doubt most would unless they suspected foul play.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://discord.gg/pte7kB6\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Moon Sept</a>, a discord server for fans of Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12874-mongoose","name":"Mongoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12874_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:59:22-08:00","id":1034571,"title":"","content":"Off-topic from the current discussion, but one thing that I've noticed a lot in games that ban lupus, is that homid are assumed to just -know- how wolf behaviour works. It is an instinct, apparently.<br /> <br /> Sadly, it is not. Like any social creature, wolves also teach a lot to their pups. This is one of the reasons why ambassador wolves are taken from their litter early, so they aren't taught how to fear humans. And ask anyone who has had an orphaned dog from the baby age without dog companions. Those dogs grow very socially blind to canine etiquette, and it actually causes them problems interacting with other dogs.<br /> <br /> A homid knows how humans work, but they won't automatically realize things like ear position or tail position meanings. Or how to hunt. They might even go by the cliche of alpha-wolf and act like a total asshole to wolves.<br /> <br /> Now, I must note that dominance and submissions in a way are instinctual. But in the sense that prisons form their own pecking order. It is not quite what most wolf packs in the wild are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:31:18-08:00","id":1034586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mongoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1034336#post1034336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's the Rite of Heritage, which can tell your parentage up to X successes per generation; e.g., two successes would reveal your parents &amp; grandparents. As for if they'd track down the parents, I suppose it depends on the Coggies involved. I doubt most would unless they suspected foul play.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But that's a Fenrir Rite. So if the Fenrir are involved, they will absolutely hunt the parents down.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I've seen people play Coggies who are very pro-First-Tenet. &quot;Yeah. The CoG fuckin' hate Metis because we have to deal with your byblows. You just punish the charach and leave us to do the actual <i>work</i>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T07:39:53-08:00","id":1034594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1034586#post1034586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, I've seen people play Coggies who are very pro-First-Tenet. &quot;Yeah. The CoG fuckin' hate Metis because we have to deal with your byblows. You just punish the charach and leave us to do the actual <i>work</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I do have this CoG Philodox Traditionalist concept floating around in my head. &quot;You keep the Litany. You respect the traditions of the tribes. Because our ancestors knew that traditions are what holds the Garou Nation together. Do not start a war because you disagree with another tribe's traditions.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T08:54:36-08:00","id":1034635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1034586#post1034586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's a Fenrir Rite. So if the Fenrir are involved, they will absolutely hunt the parents down.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I've seen people play Coggies who are very pro-First-Tenet. &quot;Yeah. The CoG fuckin' hate Metis because we have to deal with your byblows. You just punish the charach and leave us to do the actual <i>work</i>.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In W20, it's a standard rite for all tribes, or at least it makes no mention of it being exclusive to the Fenrir.<br /> <br /> And I'm a fan of that interpretation. Could be fun to to throw players up against a conservative CoG, especially if they think they're all a bunch of softies or assume they'll allow their litany violation to slide.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://discord.gg/pte7kB6\" target=\"_blank\">The Black Moon Sept</a>, a discord server for fans of Werewolf: the Apocalypse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12874-mongoose","name":"Mongoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12874_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T11:07:37-08:00","id":1034727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1034571#post1034571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off-topic from the current discussion, but one thing that I've noticed a lot in games that ban lupus, is that homid are assumed to just -know- how wolf behaviour works. It is an instinct, apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, there's plenty of that in the books. All Garou are noted as instinctively understanding their wolf side better than their human side or even spiritual side. So it's not just weird things from various ways people play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:49:57-08:00","id":1034995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1034727#post1034727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, there's plenty of that in the books. All Garou are noted as instinctively understanding their wolf side better than their human side or even spiritual side. So it's not just weird things from various ways people play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I haven't seen seen much of what you're describing, that all garou understand their wolf side better than either their human side or spiritual side. The W20 core book doesn't give that impression to me for sure. Using Primal Urge as an example again, there's a reason that ability is listed as &quot;Possessed by: Lupus, Wild Animals, Predators,&quot; rather than homid or even metis. Homids don't have any restrictions on Abilities, but it says that they are generally less intuitive and perceptive than lupus or metis, and have a weaker connection to the wolf and spirit portions of their nature. Description of the lupus breed flat out says that they have &quot;an understanding of the natural world that homids can't hope to understand.&quot; The difference is also shown mechanically given the impact that breed gifts have on each breed and what they are good at. Obviously this can change over time - a homid can catch up like a lupus can catch up to things that human born have experience with - but the starting line is very different, and it's probably very difficult to totally make up the difference.<br /> <br /> I'd also say that the issue isn't instinct as much as experience. A homid may suddenly gain the new senses and instincts, but that doesn't mean they know what to make of it. The Players Guide to Garou notes this when describing homids, that the newly changed garou suddenly experiences sharper instincts, hunches, senses, reaction speed... but that these are often a source of confusion and frustration for them at first. This is different from lupus, who have grown up with much of that already. Lupus are also already familiar with the socialization of the pack rather than a larger society, where as homid have an easier time with the former than the latter.<br /> <br /> I'm sure it probably varies by edition and book as well. The second edition core book (only using it as an example because it is right next to me) hardly talks about this even less than W20, maybe 2-3 sentences in the breed descriptions and that's it. I'm know I tend to take certain things for granted just because they make sense to me. Roleplaying the various learning curves for garou characters seems much more interesting to me than hand-waving them away, and is part of what gives the werewolf &quot;condition&quot; immediate consequences beyond their spiritual purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3533-sonofgaia","name":"SonOfGaia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T23:17:49-08:00","id":1035102,"title":"","content":"One of the big points is that all Garou speak &quot;wolf&quot; instinctively after the First Change, but none of them naturally speak human languages or even the Garou Tongue (p. 58 W20).<br /> <br /> So the second a Homid or Metis has their first change, they immediately are fluent enough in &quot;wolf&quot; to communicate effectively with normal wolves (with all the non-vocalized communication that includes). However being able to deal with human stuff is always considered a learned activity, as are Garou cultural matters, and many non-automatic powers (like rolling to shapeshift) is also something that needs training (in Primal Urge or Gnosis) to be good at. That's a pretty big message that there is a much smaller learning curve for learning to be a wolf; which I don't particularly like, but that's in the books.<br /> <br /> The point here is simply that regardless of how any of us feel about how it should be, that people doing things in a way I think most of the people in this thread disagree with are actually pulling their ideas from the books; not some weird phenomenon that plagues certain avenues of playing the game.<br /> <br /> If there's any correlation there, the kinds of games that we're talking about tend to be more heavy handed about running things by-the-book because they frequently have much larger groups of players and more than one person handling the ST role, which means compromising to whatever the book says is much easier than implementing a bunch of house rules even if everyone would probably like the house ruled version better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T04:28:02-08:00","id":1035159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1034727#post1034727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, there's plenty of that in the books. All Garou are noted as instinctively understanding their wolf side better than their human side or even spiritual side. So it's not just weird things from various ways people play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That IS true, very much so. But it is rather hilarious how homid are given much more leeway, while lupus are basically relegated to nothing more than feral children or utterly ignorant of anything human/the veil. That is my issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T05:24:03-08:00","id":1035171,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that is an ST problem. Unless you are playing a First Change game, your character should have been one of Garou for a few years before reaching Rank 1. They have been taught everything necessary to be a functional Garou, including the basics of local human culture and language if they are Lupus/Metis, and will be able to exist within Garou, Human, and Wolf society without major issues. <br /> <br /> The biggest problem that Lupus should really have is with sex as, from the limited research into the differences between human and canine sex, the pleasure experienced by humans is potentially tenfold that of canines. Even more amazing to Lupus, humans can potentially have sex all the time while canines are more restricted. There should probably be quite a few Lupus sex addicts, though I really do not think that the Garou would care as long as they do not have sex with other Garou and do not let it interfere with their duties. The worst case scenario is they produce more Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T06:39:39-08:00","id":1035190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1031969-playing-lupus-metis?p=1035171#post1035171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There should probably be quite a few Lupus sex addicts, though I really do not think that the Garou would care as long as they do not have sex with other Garou and do not let it interfere with their duties. The worst case scenario is they produce more Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the world of darkness. That's far from the worst-case scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T06:54:44-08:00","id":1035195,"title":"","content":"I always imagined homid was the shape of touch and color. Lupus was the shape of scent, sound, and night vision. Metis is somewhere in between.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}